## Summary

The opencode plugin (`src/plugins/opencode/plugin.js`) registers `session.created` as a direct top-level key in the hook object. As of opencode v1.15.6, session events are dispatched through a single `event` handler (per [opencode plugin docs](https://opencode.ai/docs/plugins#events)), and the direct key is silently ignored. Result: `.caveman-active` flag is never written on session start, so the per-prompt reinforcement in `tui.prompt.append` never fires (it reads the flag and bails when empty).

Always-on caveman in opencode only works because of the separately-installed `~/.config/opencode/AGENTS.md`. The plugin's dynamic-state layer (`tui.prompt.append` per-turn reinforcement) is silently inert.

`tui.prompt.append` still works because TUI events use the direct-key pattern. Session/lifecycle events do not.

## Reproduction

1. Fresh install: `npx -y github:JuliusBrussee/caveman -- --only opencode`
2. Delete flag: `rm -f ~/.config/opencode/.caveman-active`
3. Start opencode v1.15.6
4. Send any prompt
5. `cat ~/.config/opencode/.caveman-active` → **file does not exist**

Expected: flag should contain `full` (or the configured default mode).

## Root cause

Plugin source: https://github.com/JuliusBrussee/caveman/blob/main/src/plugins/opencode/plugin.js#L126

```js
export const CavemanPlugin = async (_ctx) => ({
  'session.created': async () => { ... },        // ← silently ignored in opencode >= 1.15
  'tui.prompt.append': async (input) => { ... }, // ← still works (TUI events use direct keys)
});
```

opencode's plugin docs ([Session Events section](https://opencode.ai/docs/plugins#events) + the "Send notifications" example showing `event: async ({ event }) => { if (event.type === "session.idle") ... }`) document that session events flow through a single `event` handler that dispatches on `event.type`.

## Fix

```js
function handleSessionCreated() {
  const mode = getDefaultMode();
  if (mode === 'off') {
    try { if (existsSync(flagPath)) unlinkSync(flagPath); } catch (e) {}
    return;
  }
  safeWriteFlag(flagPath, mode);
}

export const CavemanPlugin = async (_ctx) => ({
  event: async ({ event }) => {
    if (event && event.type === 'session.created') handleSessionCreated();
  },
  'tui.prompt.append': async (input) => { /* unchanged */ },
});
```

Patched locally; verified the flag is now written on session start and per-turn reinforcement fires.

## Environment

- opencode `1.15.6`
- macOS 25.5.0 (Darwin)
- caveman installed via official installer (`--only opencode`)

