## Bug

For Claude Code **plugin/marketplace installs**, `src/hooks/caveman-activate.js` never finds `SKILL.md` and silently falls back to the small hardcoded ruleset, so the full intensity-filtered ruleset (persistence rules, auto-clarity, wenyan modes, level switching) is never injected at SessionStart.

## Root cause

`caveman-activate.js` resolves:

```js
path.join(__dirname, '..', 'skills', 'caveman', 'SKILL.md')
```

The comment above it says plugin installs run with `__dirname = <plugin_root>/hooks/`, but in the actual marketplace-installed layout the hook lives at `<plugin_root>/src/hooks/` (there is no top-level `hooks/` dir in the repo). So the path resolves to `<plugin_root>/src/skills/caveman/SKILL.md`, which doesn't exist — the real file is at `<plugin_root>/skills/caveman/SKILL.md`. The `try/catch` then silently selects the fallback.

## Repro

From an installed plugin cache (e.g. `~/.claude/plugins/cache/caveman/caveman/<hash>/`):

```bash
echo '{}' | node src/hooks/caveman-activate.js | wc -c
```

Output is the small fallback ruleset, not the full SKILL.md content. After patching the path to `'..', '..', 'skills', ...` the full ruleset loads (verified locally).

## Suggested fix

Try the plugin layout first, keep the old path as a secondary fallback so standalone installs are unaffected:

```js
let skillContent = '';
try {
  skillContent = fs.readFileSync(
    path.join(__dirname, '..', '..', 'skills', 'caveman', 'SKILL.md'), 'utf8'
  );
} catch (e) {
  try {
    skillContent = fs.readFileSync(
      path.join(__dirname, '..', 'skills', 'caveman', 'SKILL.md'), 'utf8'
    );
  } catch (e2) { /* standalone install — fallback below */ }
}
```

