## Bug
`/caveman-stats` works in the terminal Claude Code but produces **no output** in the Claude Code macOS app. The hook fires (the per-turn caveman reminder still injects), but the stats block never appears.

## Root cause
`src/hooks/caveman-mode-tracker.js` delivers stats via `{"decision":"block","reason": <stats>}` on `UserPromptSubmit`. The terminal renders a blocked prompt's `reason`; the macOS app **honors the block (swallows the prompt) but never renders `reason`** → stats vanish silently.

## Fix
Deliver the stats via `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` instead and let the model print the block verbatim. `additionalContext` is honored by both the terminal and the app.

