## Problem

WorkBuddy (Tencent's CodeBuddy-derived agent) is not in caveman's `PROVIDERS`, so the official installer cannot enable caveman there. WorkBuddy's hook runtime supports Claude-style events (`SessionStart`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `Stop`), but its hook JSON only uses `systemMessage` — no `hookSpecificOutput` / `additionalContext`.

## Proposal

Add a `workbuddy` provider (or ship standalone hook files) that registers:

- `SessionStart` -> `hooks/workbuddy/session-start.js`
- `UserPromptSubmit` -> `hooks/workbuddy/user-prompt-submit.js`

The hooks reuse upstream `caveman-config.js` and `caveman-parse.js` from v4.2.0, keep per-session mode state under the WorkBuddy config dir, and support `/caveman`, `/ultracave`, `/megacave`, `/caveman ultra`, `/caveman wenyan`, `stop caveman`, `normal mode`, and Chinese `正常模式`.

